unresolved.message:
@Nicole Weber would that be possible to make this "X" dismiss button larger? 

It's expected that interactive target areas are to be 48dp or larger to allow users with limited dexterity and users on the go to better target and tap controls (per WCAG 2.2 Level AAA Success Criteria 2.5.5 and 2.5.8 Target Size (Enhanced and Minimum). More details could be found in BBC Accessibility guide. Usually, anything that is less than 35dp in size is flagged as "access-S2" issue by QA and Accessibility. The touch area of the button would be a bit larger than the icon itself, of course, but when the icon is that small, some users may miss it (those with 20/20 vision may miss this control too, because it is small).

Similarly to the "V" expandable caret on the "Extensions" view - while the entire row can be tapped to activate it (thus, this case won't be a severe issue, more an enhancement), the identifier of the state appears to be small visually.

